  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. A long session (WBS 8.5) of 52 inputs with one fight, against two bandits from input 24, about halfway through. Edda is not a spellcaster and has no way to heal, so whatever hit points she loses at inputs 24 to 30 stay lost for the rest of the session: inputs 32, 49 and 51 invite a hit-point band phrase 2, 19 and 21 inputs after the fight, and the night's sleep at input 51 restores nothing (no rests). Rations are the numeric thread: 3 at the start, 2 after input 7, 1 after input 18, 3 after Orlo's gift at input 35 and 2 after input 38; input 49 asks for a count. The hermit's herbs have no mechanical effect: chewing them at input 19 changes no hit points. The letter leaves the inventory at input 43 and the badge at input 40. Three quests: the caravan runs the full ladder to stage 4 and completes, the letter (max_stage 1) completes, and the mule quest fails at input 16; input 50 asks about the mule after it was given up. Three NPCs: Orlo goes up twice to allied, the toll captain up once to neutral, and the hermit down once to unfriendly. Input 46 asks for coin, and there is no currency in the game, so narration that adds money to the inventory is a PHANTOM. Inputs 24 to 30 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game. The badge is taken at input 31 even if the first bandit is still standing."
}
